WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
Over a thousand years ago, poet-saints
in South India travelled from temple to

2
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.800
temple, singing.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.860
Some sang to Vishnu, some to Shiva.

4
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.800
Among them were women, such as Andal.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.850
Many of their hymns are still
sung in Tamil temples today.

6
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:22.050
How did poems and songs let outcastes
and women reach God directly?

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.170
In this mission, you'll meet the saints
who began this movement of devotion,

8
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.080
and the gods they loved.

9
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:31.510
Then you'll explore devotion
to Vishnu and to Shiva,

10
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.340
and what it means to surrender to God.

11
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.310
Your mission: find out how songs of
devotion changed who could reach God.
